He sighs once more as you realize what he said. Japan? That’s strange. His accent gave away that he was probably from somewhere else, but you didn’t expect Japan considering… <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Considering I’m black?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> says with a raised eyebrow. <span style="color:Yellow">You quickly turn red and try to stutter out an excuse. You didn’t mean it like that!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> laughs, finding your flustered state entertaining, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s true and I don’t blame you for thinking that. I’m only half Japanese. The other half is Nigerian, on my mom’s side, and it seems those genes are dominant.”</span> He laughs, stretching out in his seat. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I moved here a few years back for… reasons.”</span> He pauses, staring off blankly, before he blinks and suddenly returns to his usual self. <span style="color:Yellow">He turns to you with a smirk and grabs you by the neck in a loose but firm choke hold.</span> <br>
